This lesson set is devoted to the streamlining of the mcu/sensors in lesson set 01
The idea is to use fewer mcus to deliver data from TWO complementary sensors instead of a single sensor.
By bringing two sensors under the control of a single mcu we reduce complexity and cost.
This also reduces the need for so many entry nodes. 
Instead of a single entry node for each sensor we can use one entry node for each complementary sensor pair.
Keep in mind that we are not looking to overwhelm the mcu but instead to improve the functionality by pairing like sensors into an array.

Additionally, by doing it in this manner we reduce the complexity of discovering the mcus from four to two.

